WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.043
Belot — Discover belote and its relatives from other countries, then play at the table: you and an AI partner against two AI opponents.

2
00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:14.186
Cărți de joc — From Solitaire and Old Maid to poker: 17 card games with explained rules, 8 of which you can also play right away.

3
00:00:14.386 --> 00:00:21.329
Dame — Play 25 draughts variants against the computer and save your game.

4
00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:28.471
Domino — Learn the history and rules of dominoes, then play at the table against one to three computer-controlled opponents.

5
00:00:28.671 --> 00:00:35.614
Go — Find out where Go comes from and how it's played, then try your hand against the computer, which can give you hints.

6
00:00:35.814 --> 00:00:42.757
Mahjong — Discover 8 mahjong variants and play solitaire or the four-player game, with three simple computer-controlled opponents.

7
00:00:42.957 --> 00:00:49.900
Profund — 150 questions that take conversation beyond small talk, between friends or in the family.

8
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:57.043
Remi — Discover the rummy family and play 19 variants against the computer, with statistics.

9
00:00:57.243 --> 00:01:04.186
Șah — Over 700 chess variants to explore, with a small dictionary of terms; for many you can play against the computer.

10
00:01:04.386 --> 00:01:11.329
Scopone — Find out how Scopone was born, what its rules are and how they differ from region to region, then play against the computer, which can give you hints.

11
00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:18.471
Solitaire — Browse solitaire games such as Klondike, FreeCell or Spider and play them.

12
00:01:18.671 --> 00:01:25.614
Sudoku — 136 kinds of Sudoku, from classic to killer or 3D, to browse and play.

13
00:01:25.814 --> 00:01:32.757
Table — Backgammon, Tavli, Narde and the Romanian variants of tabla, to read about and play: 17 variants against the computer, with keyboard or mouse.

14
00:01:32.957 --> 00:01:39.900
Zaruri — 26 dice games to read about, 12 of them playable against the computer, plus a roll simulator with probabilities.
